$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=carmswn  LOC_AFTER=?

* The algorithmic main theorem at the machine natural parameters: under the AGP hypotheses there are naturals c >= 1000 and k >= 2 such that eventually the search at the machine scales ( ( c ScTM k ) ` n ) costs at most exp ( 100 ell2 n ell3 n ) and, for every e > 0, eventually returns a certified Carmichael number in ( n , n ^c ( 1 + e ) ] (Lean: the hcost of exists_computableInTime and searchFun_spec, at C1c = ceil C1alg and Kc = max 2 ceil ( 1 / Eweak )).

